WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.027 --> 00:00:02.412
- [Voiceover] Cotton candy.

00:00:02.412 --> 00:00:05.821
Who knew sugar and air
could taste so sweet?

00:00:05.821 --> 00:00:09.364
Well, a guy named James
Morrison, an amateur inventor

00:00:09.364 --> 00:00:13.531
who's occupation and taste
buds didn't exactly align.

00:00:16.076 --> 00:00:19.208
He was a dentist and during his lifetime,

00:00:19.208 --> 00:00:21.017
James even became the President

00:00:21.017 --> 00:00:24.216
of the Tennessee Dental Association.

00:00:24.216 --> 00:00:25.499
- [Voiceover] Don't forget to floss.

00:00:25.499 --> 00:00:28.108
- [Voiceover] But he was also
a confectionary enthusiast

00:00:28.108 --> 00:00:30.441
with a passion for culinary advancement.

00:00:30.441 --> 00:00:31.980
He paired with John C. Wharton,

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.719
an old friend and fellow confectioner.

00:00:34.719 --> 00:00:36.855
Together the two designed and co-patented

00:00:36.855 --> 00:00:40.206
what they called the
electronic candy machine.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.782
The device rapidly spun and melted sugar

00:00:42.782 --> 00:00:44.808
through small holes until it was fluffy

00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:46.706
and nearly 70 percent air.

00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:49.190
They called the new treat fairy floss.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.631
They introduced their product
at the 1904 World's Fair,

00:00:52.631 --> 00:00:56.138
selling it in small wooden
boxes for 25 cents each.

00:00:56.138 --> 00:00:56.971
- [Voiceover] Thank you.

00:00:56.971 --> 00:00:58.839
- [Voiceover] That's
about six dollars today.

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:00.946
Fairy floss was a huge success.

00:01:00.946 --> 00:01:04.681
In six months, they
sold over 68,000 boxes,

00:01:04.681 --> 00:01:05.514
grossing in today's money
around 440,000 dollars.

00:01:05.514 --> 00:01:09.948
grossing in today's money
around 440,000 dollars.

00:01:09.948 --> 00:01:13.333
But despite the success of
the sugar spun business,

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:17.347
Morrison returned to his
day job as a dentist.

00:01:17.347 --> 00:01:18.820
So next time the dentist tells you

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.269
you're eating too many sugary treats,

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:22.102
well blame him.

00:01:22.102 --> 00:01:23.352
well blame him.

00:01:24.606 --> 00:01:25.439
Awkward.

